            "description": "This lab demonstrates the setup and management of cloud infrastructure using Amazon Web Services (AWS). The objective is to deploy, configure, and monitor cloud resources while following best practices for security, scalability, and cost optimization.",
            "shortDescription": "This lab demonstrates the setup and management of cloud infrastructure using Amazon Web Services (AWS). The objective is to deploy, configure, and monitor cloud resources while following best practices for security, scalability, and cost optimization.",
            "fullDescription": "Amazon Web Services (AWS) is one of the world's leading cloud computing platforms, providing a wide range of services including computing power, storage, networking, databases, security, and analytics. This AWS Cloud Computing Lab was designed to provide hands-on experience with deploying, managing, and monitoring cloud infrastructure using AWS services.\n\nThe primary goal of this lab was to understand cloud computing concepts and gain practical knowledge of creating scalable, secure, and highly available cloud environments. Throughout the lab, various AWS services were configured and integrated to simulate a real-world cloud deployment scenario.",
